WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.000
A rumored affair, a violent assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.440
and some serious allegations. Did Netflix's&nbsp;
new Marilyn Monroe feature go too far?

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.780
Netflix's "Blonde," which is based on Joyce Carol&nbsp;
Oates' novel of the same name, and stars Ana de&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.760
Armas as Marilyn Monroe, has been creating a lot&nbsp;
of controversy. Despite being a work of fiction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.260
"Blonde" has shocked audiences, because it draws&nbsp;
inspiration from one of Hollywood's most iconic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:27.360
figures, and as it received an NC-17 rating,&nbsp;
meaning that it contains several shocking scenes.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.560
The fictionalized account of Monroe's life&nbsp;
explores the possible trauma, failures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.400
successes, and intense pressure the "Some Like It&nbsp;
Hot" star might have faced throughout her life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.660
Viewers are given an imagined behind-the-scenes&nbsp;
look at what the world's most famous stars face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.900
examining the human being inside&nbsp;
the gilded veneer of the myth.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.660
While it's true that some people&nbsp;
want nothing more than to be famous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.400
others come to rue such a bright spotlight.&nbsp;
Since "Blonde" draws inspiration from the life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.000
of a historical figure, several other&nbsp;
real-life people associated with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.180
star also feature in the fictional&nbsp;
account. However, not everyone is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:02.280
shown in a flattering light. Discussing the&nbsp;
film's NC-17 rating, de Armas told Empire,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.400
"It's a film that is supposed to&nbsp;
create controversy and discomfort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.800
and it's supposed to make you&nbsp;
think about what happened — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.100
what is still happening [...] It's&nbsp;
revolutionary, and I think it's so brave."

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.820
The actor also pointed out that&nbsp;
although "Blonde" is rated NC-17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.720
she doesn't consider the movie's&nbsp;
content particularly gratuitous, saying,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.280
"Despite the NC-17 rating, I never felt that&nbsp;
there was anything exploitative [...] This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.040
movie is meant to be an experience,&nbsp;
to move along with her feelings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.220
what she's going through. And that,&nbsp;
unfortunately, takes what it takes."

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.540
However, it quickly became clear that "Blonde"&nbsp;
features one especially gut-wrenching scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.740
that's harrowing and deeply uncomfortable for&nbsp;
both viewers and history aficionados alike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.540
According to The Daily Beast, this particular&nbsp;
scene in "Blonde" focuses on Marilyn Monroe and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.740
John F. Kennedy, played by Caspar Phillipson.&nbsp;
The moment begins with Monroe being picked up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.820
by secret service agents from an airplane in&nbsp;
New York City. The actress is then dragged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.360
through a hotel and presented to Kennedy,&nbsp;
and that's when the story becomes shocking.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.920
"I'm not a child. You don't&nbsp;
have to worry about me."

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.560
In Netflix's fictional account, Kennedy&nbsp;
sexually assaults Monroe multiple times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.540
which is understandably difficult for audiences&nbsp;
to watch. In the movie, when Monroe wakes up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.200
she is bloody and bruised. However,&nbsp;
presidential historians will likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.780
take exception with how the alleged&nbsp;
relationship between the president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.740
and the film star has been presented.&nbsp;
Obviously, it has long been rumored that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.940
the real-life Kennedy and Monroe had some kind&nbsp;
of relationship with one another. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:28.620
Frank Sinatra's friend Tony Oppedisano opened up&nbsp;
to People about the possible connection, alleging,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.820
"It was obviously a sexual thing, and I would&nbsp;
expect that there were feelings on her side.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.300
Just taking a look at the footage of her&nbsp;
singing her 'Happy Birthday,' that speaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.260
for itself. [...] She respected him; she admired&nbsp;
him. She loved what he was doing with the country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.220
and then to have a physical relationship with&nbsp;
him, she found him attractive and vice versa."

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.600
However, not everyone agrees that Monroe and&nbsp;
Kennedy were actually engaged in any sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:53.580
illicit affair. As a result, many historians&nbsp;
will likely find fault with Netflix's "Blonde,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.780
and the devastating suggestion that Monroe&nbsp;
was assaulted by the president. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.720
it's crucial to remember that the&nbsp;
new film is based upon a novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.680
and not a biography. Whether or not&nbsp;
Kennedy and Monroe were romantically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.000
linked in real life, "Blonde" continues to&nbsp;
shock viewers due to its explicit content.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.240
If you or anyone you know has&nbsp;
been a victim of sexual assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.140
help is available. Visit the Rape,&nbsp;
Abuse &amp; Incest National Network&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:23.040
website or contact RAINN's National&nbsp;
Helpline at 1-800-656-HOPE (4673).

